-- ProvinceDim: one row per province, combining provinces seen in stores and in leads
-- Shared dimension pattern: avoids a many-to-many relationship between leads and stores.
-- Create in Power BI: Modelling ribbon -> New table -> paste this DAX.
ProvinceDim =
DISTINCT (
    UNION (
        VALUES ( stores[province] ),              -- 7 trading provinces
        VALUES ( marketing_leads_clean[province] ) -- 4 lead provinces
    )
)

-- Expected result: 7 rows
-- Eastern Cape, Free State, Gauteng, KwaZulu-Natal, Limpopo, Mpumalanga, Western Cape
--
-- Then in Model view:
--   ProvinceDim[Province] 1 -> * stores[province]
--   ProvinceDim[Province] 1 -> * marketing_leads_clean[province]
-- Both single-direction (ProvinceDim filters outward).
-- Delete any auto-created relationship between leads and stores.
